The exact package names keep changing so do a apt search ocl

sudo apt install ocl-icd-libopencl1
sudo apt install opencl-headers
sudo apt install clinfo

sudo apt install ocl-icd-opencl-dev

## Intel only (older chips)
sudo apt install beignet
## Newer chips are supported by the Intel official OpenCL runtime

=========
There is pocl which is fairly decent for the CPU implementation

__BUT__ for CPU you really want the Intel Xeon implementation, the backend and vectorization is orders of magnitude faster
than the Open Source versions


Also to switch between OpenCL ICD vendors, goto /etc/OpenCL/vendors and hide the vendor.icd file. Verify with clinfo
